    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What kinds of commercial projects do you take on?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We take on a range of commercial work across North Jersey, with a focus on interior build-outs and renovations rather than ground-up towers. That includes retail and office build-outs, restaurant and food-service spaces, tenant improvements for new leases, and general commercial renovations. Whether you're a landlord preparing a vacant unit for a new tenant, a business owner fitting out a first location, or an established operator modernizing a tired space, we can manage it. Commercial projects come with their own layer of requirements — commercial building codes, ADA accessibility, fire and life-safety systems, and coordination across multiple trades — and we're set up to handle that coordination and keep everything compliant. We work with you or your architect from plans through final inspection and certificate of occupancy. If you're not sure whether your project fits what we do, reach out and describe it, and we'll give you a straight answer about whether we're the right team for it."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you work around our business hours?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, and for an operating business this is often the single most important part of the job. We know that every day your doors are closed or your space is torn up is lost revenue, so we plan the work around keeping you running. That means phasing and sequencing the project so we work in sections while the rest of your space stays open, and going after-hours or overnight where it makes sense to keep customer-facing areas clear during business hours. For a retail store, that might mean building out the back while the front stays open; for a restaurant or office, it might mean concentrating the disruptive work into nights or a planned closure window we agree on in advance. We'll map out a schedule built around your operations, not just our convenience, and communicate clearly about which areas are affected and when — so you can plan staffing, deliveries and customers around the work."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you handle permits and inspections?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. We manage permitting, inspections, and code compliance across all the trades involved in your project. Commercial work carries a heavier regulatory load than residential — commercial building codes, fire and life-safety requirements, ADA accessibility, and often health-department review for food-service spaces — and each of those can involve its own permits and inspections. We coordinate the whole process: pulling the permits, scheduling inspections at the right phases for structural, electrical, plumbing, mechanical, and fire-protection work, and making sure everything passes so you can reach your certificate of occupancy without last-minute surprises. This matters because a commercial space can't legally open — and your lease clock and revenue are ticking — until it's signed off. Handling the permitting and inspection coordination ourselves keeps the trades aligned and the approvals moving, so you're not chasing the town or discovering a missed inspection at the worst possible moment. If you're working with an architect or your own plans, we build to those and manage the compliance side around them."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are you licensed and insured for commercial work?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. We're licensed (NJ HIC #13VH12093400) and fully insured for commercial projects, and we carry the kind of coverage that landlords and tenants typically require before work can begin. Commercial jobs almost always come with insurance requirements written into the lease or building rules — commonly general liability coverage at specified limits, and often naming the property owner or management company as an additional insured on the certificate. We're set up to provide that documentation up front, so your project isn't held up waiting on paperwork and the building owner is comfortable letting work proceed. Being properly licensed and insured also protects you directly: on a commercial site with multiple trades and the public nearby, the liability exposure is real, and you want a contractor whose coverage stands behind the work. We're glad to share proof of insurance and credentials during bidding, and to work with your property manager's specific requirements so the project starts cleanly and stays compliant from the first day through final sign-off."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long will our project take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on the scope of the work and on the approval timelines, which in commercial projects can be as significant as the construction itself. A straightforward office refresh or a small retail build-out can move quickly, while a full restaurant build with kitchen equipment, grease and ventilation systems, and health-department review takes considerably longer. The permitting and inspection phase is often the biggest variable — commercial approvals involve more agencies and more sign-offs than residential work, and that runway has to be planned for, not assumed away. Rather than quote an optimistic number we can't hold to, we give you a realistic schedule with your quote that accounts for both the approval process and the construction sequence, and we keep you updated against it as the job progresses. For a business, a schedule you can actually plan around — staffing, an opening date, lease timing — is worth far more than a fast number that slips, so we set expectations we can meet."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you serve?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We serve businesses throughout North Jersey, centered on our base in Wayne and the surrounding Bergen, Passaic, Morris and Essex County area. That includes the commercial corridors and downtowns across both counties — retail spaces, offices, restaurants, and mixed-use buildings within a comfortable working radius of home. Staying regional is deliberate: it keeps our crews close to your site, lets us respond quickly when a question or an inspection comes up, and means we already know the local building departments and their commercial permit and inspection processes, which is a real advantage when your opening date depends on approvals moving on schedule. It also lets us be on site and responsive throughout the job rather than stretched thin across distant projects. If your business is in or near Bergen or Passaic County and you're not certain we cover your location, just reach out with the address — we'll confirm quickly and, if it's a fit, set up a time to walk the space and scope the work."
          }
        }
      ],
